{
  "name": "Coals",
  "created": "2026-09-13T18:00:00.000Z",
  "notes": "The fire after it has burned down. A dim crimson bed that barely moves, and over it a second, finer noise whose palette is BLACK for most of its range -- black here means off -- so only its crests light, glowing orange-to-gold where the coals are hottest. Heat is that layer's `indexBias`: turn it up and more of each coal catches.\n\nThe crests breathe on a slow sine into the same `indexBias`, and a perlin LFO drives that sine's rate, so the glow swells and settles irregularly instead of on a count. A fast, shallow perlin shimmers the crest layer's opacity -- heat haze, not flicker. The bed and the crests drift in opposite directions at very different speeds, so the hot spots slide over the embers rather than sitting on them.",
